rability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.02557500522076392,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":75.6,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.36607070557865673,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.2559394483552495,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.05018275085367479,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":16.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.01588,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":10.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.75,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":75.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Tilray Brands, Inc., a lifestyle consumer products company, engages in the research, cultivation, processing, and distribution of medical cannabis products in Canada, the United States, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and internationally. The company operates through four segments: Beverage, Cannabis, Distribution, and Wellness. It also offers medical and adult-use cannabis products; resells and distributes pharmaceutical and wellness products; and produces, markets, and sells beverage products, and hemp-based food products. In addition, the company provides entertainment products. It offers its products under the Tilray, Aphria, Broken Coast, Symbios, Navcora, Tilray Craft, Charlotte's Web, Shock Top, Montauk Brewing, 10 Barrell, Breckenridge Brewery, SweetWater Brewing, Breckenridge Distillery, Blue Point, Alpine, Broken Coast, Redecan, XMG, Manitoba Harvest, CC Pharma, Good Supply, Solei, Mollo, Chowie Wowie, Original Stash, Canaca, RIFF, Tilray Medical, Bake Sale, The Batch, HEXO, Cruisies, Atwater Brewery, Hi-ball Energy, Liquid Love, Hop Valley Brewing, Redhook Brewery, Revolver Brewing, Square Mile Cider, Mock One, Widmer Brothers Brewing, Runner's High Brewing Company, SweetWater Brewing Company, Terrapin brands. The company sells its products to retailers, wholesalers, patients, physicians, hospitals, pharmacies, researchers, and governments, as well as direct to consumers. The company was formerly known as Tilray, Inc. and changed its name to Tilray Brands, Inc. in January 2022. Tilray Brands, Inc. is headquartered in Leamington, Canada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Irwin David Simon | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 67 | Compensation: $3.3M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $255K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 47%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $13K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 13\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Recent headlines include layoff or workforce-reduction announcements.","financial_summary":["Tilray Brands, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $432M market cap on $915M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -14% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 24% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","On the balance sheet, thin -2.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 36.6% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-2.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 179% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.7855212355212355},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Healthcare peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Recent layoff news \u2014 often the market\u2019s first signal that growth is under pressure or costs are being rebased","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Is Driving Tilray Brands\u2019 (NASDAQ:TLRY) Record Revenue Growth?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/cannabis/what-is-driving-tilray-brands-nasdaqtlry-record-revenue-growth","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793909640.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.452,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Tilray Brands, Inc. (TLRY) is Attracting Investor Attention: Here is What You Should Know","source":"zacks.co